      "heading": "B — Audience, level and prerequisites: special driving conditions",
      "learner_facing": false,
      "markdown": "## B — Audience, level and prerequisites: special driving conditions\nAudience: first-time Missouri Class F applicants, from teens on an instruction permit to adult newcomers, who have little or no experience in darkness, winter weather or emergencies.\nWhy it matters to a first-timer: beam distances and headlight rules are exact test items [A01], snow, ice and hydroplaning guidance has exact gaps and speeds [A02], and emergency responses are ordered steps that are easy to get backwards [A04].\nLevel: rule recall plus ordered emergency procedures with several look-alike responses; moderate to high load.\nPrerequisites: the everyday safe driving chapter on following distance and stopping distance.\n",
